# Files and folders that chezmoi deletes from your home folder when it applies
# the dotfiles, if they exist. Each line is a path in your home folder, written
# without the ~/. (This file is read as a template, like .chezmoiignore.)
#
# Earlier versions of these dotfiles configured zsh; the shell setup now lives
# in fish (~/.config/fish). These are the files those versions wrote, so that
# other machines drop them on their next `chezmoi update`. On a Mac, the same
# apply writes the new ~/.zprofile, which isn't listed here. Your own files are
# left alone: ~/.config/zsh/.zshrc.local (install.sh reminds you to move it to
# fish) and zsh's history in ~/.local/state/zsh.
.zshenv
.config/zsh/.zshenv
.config/zsh/.zprofile
.config/zsh/.zshrc
.config/zsh/.zlogin
.config/zsh/.zlogout
.config/zsh/completions
.config/zsh/themes
.cache/zsh
